-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.X64.Allocate.adam - x86_64 register allocation (PLAN-ADAM M6 O18)

  AllocateFunction  rewrites a selected MachineFunction (Adam.X64.Select)
                    in place: no virtual register is left, every slot and
                    argument area is a place off the stack pointer, the
                    prologue and the epilogues are in, and the function
                    holds its frame (MachineFunction.Frame) for unwind data.

  Linear scan over lifetime intervals with interval splitting (Wimmer and
  Moessenboeck, "Optimized Interval Splitting in a Linear Scan Register
  Allocator"; Wimmer and Franz carry it to SSA form), at every @optimize
  level: one allocator (debug's locals stay in slots, DESIGN sec 5, so its
  virtual registers are temporaries). Selection's code is two-address and
  gives a phi its value by copies on the edges, so a virtual register may be
  written more than once: the intervals come from a liveness of the virtual
  registers over the blocks.

  Positions: the blocks are numbered in reverse postorder from the entry
  (then the blocks no edge reaches, in their order); instruction g of that
  order reads its operands at 2g and writes at 2g + 1. An interval is a
  sorted list of ranges [from, to) (holes where the value is dead or lives in
  blocks numbered elsewhere) and the positions it is used at; every use needs
  a register. A physical register selection names (an argument, a result, rcx
  of a shift, a call's volatile set) is a fixed interval: ranges from each
  write to its last read, a write nothing reads (a call's clobber) holding
  its write position alone. A value an instruction only reads may share a
  register the instruction writes (it is read first); one it writes may not.
  No physical register is live into a block other than the entry (selection
  keeps those lifetimes inside a block); one that is raises.

  The walk takes the intervals by start. Free (no active interval holds the
  register, no inactive or fixed one meets the current before then): the
  first free hint (the register its value is in just before it, its physical
  one, then where the value a copy moves into it is and where the value it is
  copied into is; a join's value, written by more than one copy, tries the
  copy out first), then a volatile register,
  then a callee-saved one already saved, then a fresh callee-saved one, which
  is priced: taken only by an interval of ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SAVE_USES uses or
  more (below that the store and reload around a call cost what the push and
  pop do). Free for a part only, the interval is split where it stops being
  free and the rest walks on. Blocked: the register whose holders are used
  furthest ahead is taken from them (each split before the current's start,
  kept in its slot up to its next use, the rest walking on), unless every
  register is needed no later than the current's first use: then the current
  waits in its slot up to that use. A part holding no use stays in the slot.
  Splits fall between instructions (an operand read and written keeps one
  place), never between a block's closing jumps. Vector registers come from
  the ABI's volatile set first, then its callee-saved set (a float live
  across a call stays in a callee-saved one, saved by the prologue).

  A virtual register has at most one spill slot (8 bytes, after the
  function's own slots), made the first time a part of it is in memory.
  Where two parts of a value meet inside a block a move joins them before the
  instruction; on an edge the value's place at the end of the predecessor is
  compared with its place at the start of the successor, for every value
  live into it, and the edge's moves run as one parallel move: stores first,
  then the register moves in an order that reads each register before it is
  written (a cycle broken through one value's slot), reloads last. The phi
  copies selection makes are moves too: their hints make most of them moves
  of a register into itself. An edge's moves go at the end of a predecessor
  with one successor (before its closing jumps), else at the start of a
  successor with one predecessor (never the entry), else in a new block on
  the edge, after every other block (so no scope's range takes it in), the
  predecessor's jumps sent to it. A block that falls through gets a jump to
  the next block first, an empty last block a nop; a jump before a block's
  closing jumps raises.

  A value live into a block no edge reaches (a catching scope's target, which
  the unwinder enters with the callee-saved registers the call had and none
  of the moves an edge would run) lives in its slot: for each instruction
  that names it it gets a register, loaded from the slot before the
  instruction when read and stored into it after when written, so the slot
  holds its value wherever the scope raises.

  A callee-saved register an interval is given or selection writes (rdi / rsi
  of a rep movsb, as an operand or an implicit register) is saved: the
  prologue pushes each, in the ABI's order, before it reserves the frame, and
  each ret pops them in reverse after the release. A callee-saved vector
  register is saved whole (movaps) into the frame's vector area
  (FrameLayout.VectorBase) right after the reservation, each a prologue step
  (the unwinder restores it), and restored before each ret's release.

  The frame comes from the ABI part's frame rule (LayoutFrame): the locals
  are the slots in order, each at its alignment; the outgoing area is the
  largest call's; the saved registers are counted. The prologue reserves
  AllocBytes (sub rsp, after the pushes, all marked as prologue), each ret
  is preceded by its release (add rsp) and the pops. The bases resolve to the
  stack pointer after the prologue: a slot at its place, the incoming area at
  the frame's EntryBase, the outgoing area at 0.

  A slot aligned above the ABI's StackAlign realigns the frame (the ABI's
  FrameLayout.Realign): the ABI's FrameRegister is saved with the others
  (never given to an interval: it is the frame's), the prologue ends mov
  frame, rsp (its step) then and rsp, -Realign; the incoming area is off the
  frame register, and each ret's release is lea rsp, [frame + AllocBytes].
  The ABI realigning without a slot asking for it (or the reverse) raises.

  A probed frame (the ABI's FrameLayout.ProbeBytes) calls the stack probe
  (Adam.X64.Probe) after the pushes and before the reservation: mov size,
  ProbeBytes; call the probe (its registers its implicit writes). Neither is
  a prologue step (they move no stack pointer and save nothing). A probe
  register live into the function (an argument in it) raises.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.X64.Allocate;

import System.SysUtils, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Backend.Parts, Adam.X64.Registers,
  Adam.X64.Machine, Adam.X64.Probe;

public const
  // A spill slot's size and alignment: one general register, or a float64 in a vector one
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES: int64 = 8;
  // A saved callee-saved vector register's place in the frame: the whole xmm register
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_VECTOR_SAVE_BYTES: int64 = 16;
  // The uses an interval needs to be given a callee-saved register the function does not
  // save yet (see the header)
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SAVE_USES: int64 = 3;
  // The copies a hint is followed through to a value that already has its place (a
  // parallel copy's temporaries put one between a phi's value and the copy that reads it)
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_HINT_HOPS: int64 = 4;
  // A position past every instruction: no use, no meeting
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER: int64 = 4611686018427387904;
  // A value's place beside a physical register (0 or more): its spill slot, or nowhere
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT: int64 = -1;
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE: int64 = -2;
  // The walk's steps allowed per instruction and virtual register (a walk past them is a
  // broken invariant, raised rather than run forever)
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_WALK_FACTOR: int64 = 64;
  // Raised (an invariant broken) by a function allocation cannot take
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_TWICE: string = "X64 allocate: already allocated: ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_REGISTER: string = "X64 allocate: the arch has no register '";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_FREE: string = "X64 allocate: no register for ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_PLACE: string = "X64 allocate: no place for ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_SPLIT: string = "X64 allocate: a split outside its interval: ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_ORDER: string = "X64 allocate: an interval behind the walk: ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_WALK: string = "X64 allocate: the walk does not end: ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_INNER_JUMP: string = "X64 allocate: a jump before the end of m";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_LIVE_IN: string = "X64 allocate: a register live into m";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_FRAME_REGISTER: string =
    "X64 allocate: the ABI's frame register is not a callee-saved general register: ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_REALIGN: string =
    "X64 allocate: the ABI's frame and the locals' alignment disagree on realigning ";
  ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_PROBE_LIVE: string =
    "X64 allocate: a stack probe register live into the function: ";

// True for a jump to a block (jmp, jcc)
func DoIsJump(const AOp: X64Op): bool;
begin
  return (AOp = X64Op.Jmp) or (AOp = X64Op.Jcc);
end;

// AValue (0 or more) rounded up to a multiple of AAlign (1 or more)
func DoRoundUp(const AValue: int64; const AAlign: int64): int64;
begin
  return ((AValue + AAlign - 1) div AAlign) * AAlign;
end;

// The read position of the instruction position APos (0 or more) belongs to
func DoEven(const APos: int64): int64;
begin
  return (APos div 2) * 2;
end;

// The virtual register AOperand names (itself, or its memory base); -1 for none
func DoVRegOf(const AOperand: ref MachineOperand): int64;
begin
  if AOperand.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg then
    return AOperand.Reg;
  end;
  if (AOperand.Kind = OperandKind.Memory) and (AOperand.Base = MemoryBase.Register) and
    AOperand.BaseVirtual then
    return AOperand.Reg;
  end;
  return -1;
end;

// The register references of an instruction: two per operand, 2 * K operand K's register
// or memory base, 2 * K + 1 its memory index; how many AInstr has
func DoRefCount(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr): int64;
begin
  return 2 * AInstr.OperandCount;
end;

// The virtual register reference ARef of AInstr names; -1 for none
func DoRefVReg(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const ARef: int64): int64;
var
  LOperand: ref MachineOperand;
begin
  LOperand := AInstr.OperandAt(ARef div 2);
  if (ARef mod 2) = 0 then
    return DoVRegOf(LOperand);
  end;
  if (LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.Memory) and (LOperand.Scale > 0) and LOperand.IndexVirtual then
    return LOperand.IndexReg;
  end;
  return -1;
end;

// True when reference ARef of AInstr is read (a memory index always is, as its base)
func DoRefReads(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const ARef: int64): bool;
begin
  return X64OperandReads(AInstr, ARef div 2);
end;

// True when reference ARef of AInstr is a register it writes (never a memory index)
func DoRefWrites(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const ARef: int64): bool;
begin
  return ((ARef mod 2) = 0) and X64OperandWrites(AInstr, ARef div 2);
end;

// The first position both range lists hold (each ascending, disjoint [from, to) ranges in
// two lists), the first read from its range AFirst on; ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER when they never
// meet
func DoMeet(const AFroms: ref Int64List; const ATos: ref Int64List; const AFirst: int64;
  const AOtherFroms: ref Int64List; const AOtherTos: ref Int64List): int64;
var
  LI: int64;
  LJ: int64;
begin
  LI := AFirst;
  LJ := 0;
  while (LI < AFroms.Count) and (LJ < AOtherFroms.Count) do
    if ATos[LI] <= AOtherFroms[LJ] then
      LI := LI + 1;
      skip;
    end;
    if AOtherTos[LJ] <= AFroms[LI] then
      LJ := LJ + 1;
      skip;
    end;
    // The two ranges overlap: from the later start on
    if AFroms[LI] > AOtherFroms[LJ] then
      return AFroms[LI];
    end;
    return AOtherFroms[LJ];
  end;
  return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
end;

// AList's values in reverse order, as a new list
func DoReversed(const AList: ref Int64List): ref Int64List;
var
  LReversed: ref Int64List;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LReversed := ref Int64List();
  for LI := AList.Count - 1 downto 0 do
    LReversed.Add(AList[LI]);
  end;
  return LReversed;
end;

// AValue put into AList right after AAfter (which is in it)
func DoInsertAfter(const AList: ref Int64List; const AAfter: int64; const AValue: int64);
var
  LAt: int64;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LAt := AList.IndexOf(AAfter) + 1;
  AList.Add(AValue);
  for LI := AList.Count - 1 downto LAt + 1 do
    AList[LI] := AList[LI - 1];
  end;
  AList[LAt] := AValue;
end;

type
  // A block's old instructions, or the function's in numbering order (per-register sets
  // are System.SysUtils' BoolArray / Int64Array)
  InstrArray = array of ref MachineInstr;
  // A set of virtual registers, 64 to a word
  BitWords = array of uint64;
  ListArray = array of ref Int64List;

  // A lifetime interval of one virtual register, or a part split off one (see the header)
  LiveInterval = object
    VReg: int64;
    IsVector: bool;
    // Its ranges [Froms[i], Tos[i]), ascending and disjoint (descending while built)
    Froms: ref Int64List;
    Tos: ref Int64List;
    // The positions it is used at, ascending (descending while built)
    Uses: ref Int64List;
    // Its register (-1: none), or its place is its virtual register's spill slot
    Reg: int64;
    InSlot: bool;

    init(const AVReg: int64; const AIsVector: bool);
    begin
      self.VReg := AVReg;
      self.IsVector := AIsVector;
      self.Froms := ref Int64List();
      self.Tos := ref Int64List();
      self.Uses := ref Int64List();
      self.Reg := -1;
      self.InSlot := false;
    end;

    // Its first position
    const method Start(): int64;
    begin
      return self.Froms[0];
    end;

    // The position after its last
    const method Finish(): int64;
    begin
      return self.Tos[self.Tos.Count - 1];
    end;

    // True when one of its ranges holds APos
    const method Covers(const APos: int64): bool;
    var
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LMid: int64;
    begin
      LLow := 0;
      LHigh := self.Froms.Count - 1;
      while LLow <= LHigh do
        LMid := (LLow + LHigh) div 2;
        if APos < self.Froms[LMid] then
          LHigh := LMid - 1;
        else
          if APos >= self.Tos[LMid] then
            LLow := LMid + 1;
          else
            return true;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // Its first use at APos or after; ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER for none
    const method UseFrom(const APos: int64): int64;
    var
      LLow: int64;
      LHigh: int64;
      LMid: int64;
    begin
      // The first index whose use is APos or after, in [LLow, LHigh)
      LLow := 0;
      LHigh := self.Uses.Count;
      while LLow < LHigh do
        LMid := (LLow + LHigh) div 2;
        if self.Uses[LMid] < APos then
          LLow := LMid + 1;
        else
          LHigh := LMid;
        end;
      end;
      if LLow < self.Uses.Count then
        return self.Uses[LLow];
      end;
      return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
    end;

    // The first start of a range at APos or after; ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER for none
    const method RangeFrom(const APos: int64): int64;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.Froms.Count - 1 do
        if self.Froms[LI] >= APos then
          return self.Froms[LI];
        end;
      end;
      return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
    end;
  end;

  IntervalArray = array of ref LiveInterval;

  // Moves of values between places (a register, or ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT: the value's
  // spill slot): one edge's or one position's, unordered as gathered, in order once
  // sequenced (Allocator.DoSequence)
  MoveList = object
    VRegs: ref Int64List;
    Froms: ref Int64List;
    Tos: ref Int64List;

    init();
    begin
      self.VRegs := ref Int64List();
      self.Froms := ref Int64List();
      self.Tos := ref Int64List();
    end;

    // AVReg moved from place AFrom to place ATo, after the others
    method Add(const AVReg: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64);
    begin
      self.VRegs.Add(AVReg);
      self.Froms.Add(AFrom);
      self.Tos.Add(ATo);
    end;

    // How many moves it holds
    const method Count(): int64;
    begin
      return self.VRegs.Count;
    end;
  end;

  MoveArray = array of ref MoveList;

  // One function's allocation (see the header)
  Allocator = object
    hidden FFunction: ref MachineFunction;
    hidden FRegisterTable: ref X64Registers;
    hidden FAbi: ref AbiPart;
    hidden FFrame: ref FrameLayout;
    // The stack pointer's number, and how many registers the arch has
    hidden FStack: int64;
    hidden FRegisters: int64;
    // A realigned frame's frame register (the ABI's FrameRegister), -1 when the frame is
    // not realigned
    hidden FFrameReg: int64;
    // The registers an interval may be given, by class, in the order they are preferred
    // (general: the ABI's volatile ones then its callee-saved ones, the stack pointer and a
    // realigned frame's register left out; vector: the volatile ones then the callee-saved)
    hidden FGeneral: ref Int64List;
    hidden FVector: ref Int64List;
    // Per physical register: volatile, callee-saved, saved by the function so far
    hidden FIsVolatile: BoolArray;
    hidden FIsCallee: BoolArray;
    hidden FSavedNow: BoolArray;
    // The callee-saved general registers the function writes, in the ABI's order: the
    // prologue pushes them in this order, each ret pops them in the reverse
    hidden FSaved: ref Int64List;
    // The callee-saved vector registers it writes, in the ABI's order: the prologue stores
    // the k-th at the frame's VectorBase + 16 * k, each ret reloads it from there
    hidden FSavedVector: ref Int64List;
    // The blocks selection made (the edge blocks of the resolution come after them), each
    // one's successors (in the order its jumps name them) and how many predecessors it has
    hidden FBlockCount: int64;
    hidden FSuccs: ListArray;
    hidden FPredCount: Int64Array;
    // Each block's first closing jump (its instruction count when it ends in none)
    hidden FTrail: Int64Array;
    // The numbering (see the header): the blocks in order; per block its first
    // instruction's number and its positions [FFrom, FTo); per instruction number the
    // instruction and its block
    hidden FOrder: ref Int64List;
    hidden FFirst: Int64Array;
    hidden FFrom: Int64Array;
    hidden FTo: Int64Array;
    hidden FInstrs: InstrArray;
    hidden FBlockOf: Int64Array;
    hidden FInstrCount: int64;
    // The virtual registers live into and out of each block (block * FWords + word)
    hidden FWords: int64;
    hidden FLiveIn: BitWords;
    hidden FLiveOut: BitWords;
    // The virtual registers kept in their slot (live into a block no edge reaches)
    hidden FResident: BoolArray;
    // Per physical register its fixed intervals' ranges (ascending) and the walk's cursor
    // into them; the registers live into the entry; those selection writes
    hidden FFixedFroms: ListArray;
    hidden FFixedTos: ListArray;
    hidden FFixedCursor: Int64Array;
    hidden FEntryLive: BoolArray;
    hidden FFixedWritten: BoolArray;
    // The intervals; per virtual register its root interval (-1: none), its parts by start,
    // its hints (a physical register; the virtual one copied into it at a copy's read
    // position; the virtual one it is copied into at that copy's write position), how many
    // copies write it (a join's value has one per edge) and its spill slot (-1: none yet)
    hidden FIntervals: IntervalArray;
    hidden FIntervalCount: int64;
    hidden FRootOf: Int64Array;
    hidden FPartsOf: ListArray;
    hidden FHintReg: Int64Array;
    hidden FHintVReg: Int64Array;
    hidden FHintAt: Int64Array;
    hidden FHintOut: Int64Array;
    hidden FHintOutAt: Int64Array;
    hidden FCopiesIn: Int64Array;
    hidden FSlotOf: Int64Array;
    // The walk: the intervals still to take (a heap by start), the active and the inactive
    // ones, the current position and the steps taken
    hidden FHeap: ref Int64List;
    hidden FActive: ref Int64List;
    hidden FInactive: ref Int64List;
    hidden FWalkPos: int64;
    hidden FSteps: int64;
    // The moves, sequenced: before an instruction (by number), at a block's start, at a
    // block's end (before its closing jumps)
    hidden FMovesBefore: MoveArray;
    hidden FMovesStart: MoveArray;
    hidden FMovesEnd: MoveArray;
    // The edge blocks the resolution adds: each block, the block it jumps on to, its node
    // and its moves
    hidden FEdgeBlocks: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeTargets: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeNodes: ref Int64List;
    hidden FEdgeMoves: MoveArray;
    // Per block: the targets of its jumps sent to an edge block instead, and that block
    hidden FRetargetFrom: ListArray;
    hidden FRetargetTo: ListArray;

    init(const AFunction: ref MachineFunction; const AAbi: ref AbiPart);
    begin
      self.FFunction := AFunction;
      self.FRegisterTable := ref X64Registers();
      self.FAbi := AAbi;
      self.FFrame := nil;
      self.FFrameReg := -1;
      self.FStack := -1;
      self.FRegisters := 0;
      self.FGeneral := ref Int64List();
      self.FVector := ref Int64List();
      self.FSaved := ref Int64List();
      self.FSavedVector := ref Int64List();
      self.FBlockCount := 0;
      self.FOrder := ref Int64List();
      self.FInstrCount := 0;
      self.FWords := 1;
      self.FIntervalCount := 0;
      self.FHeap := ref Int64List();
      self.FActive := ref Int64List();
      self.FInactive := ref Int64List();
      self.FWalkPos := 0;
      self.FSteps := 0;
      self.FEdgeBlocks := ref Int64List();
      self.FEdgeTargets := ref Int64List();
      self.FEdgeNodes := ref Int64List();
    end;

    // The arch's number of the register named AName; raises for a name it lacks
    hidden method DoPhysical(const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LNumber: int64;
    begin
      LNumber := self.FRegisterTable.NumberOf(AName);
      if LNumber < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_REGISTER + AName + "'");
      end;
      return LNumber;
    end;

    // The stack pointer and the number of registers
    hidden method DoRegisters();
    begin
      self.FStack := self.DoPhysical(ADAM_X64_STACK_POINTER);
      self.FRegisters := self.FRegisterTable.Count();
    end;

    // The candidates by class (FGeneral, FVector) and the volatile / callee-saved marks
    hidden method DoCandidates();
    var
      LNames: StringArray;
      LNumber: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      setlength(self.FIsVolatile, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FIsCallee, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FSavedNow, self.FRegisters);
      for LI := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        self.FIsVolatile[LI] := false;
        self.FIsCallee[LI] := false;
        self.FSavedNow[LI] := false;
      end;
      LNames := self.FAbi.Volatile();
      for LI := 0 to len(LNames) - 1 do
        LNumber := self.DoPhysical(LNames[LI]);
        self.FIsVolatile[LNumber] := true;
        if LNumber >= ADAM_X64_FIRST_XMM then
          self.FVector.Add(LNumber);
        else
          if (LNumber <> self.FStack) and (LNumber <> self.FFrameReg) then
            self.FGeneral.Add(LNumber);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      // The callee-saved ones after the volatile ones (the walk tries them in this order)
      LNames := self.FAbi.CalleeSaved();
      for LI := 0 to len(LNames) - 1 do
        LNumber := self.DoPhysical(LNames[LI]);
        self.FIsCallee[LNumber] := true;
        if LNumber >= ADAM_X64_FIRST_XMM then
          self.FVector.Add(LNumber);
        else
          if (LNumber <> self.FStack) and (LNumber <> self.FFrameReg) then
            self.FGeneral.Add(LNumber);
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The largest alignment of the function's own slots (selection's: the spill slots come
    // later, at 8)
    hidden method DoSlotAlign(): int64;
    var
      LAlign: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAlign := 1;
      for LI := 0 to self.FFunction.SlotCount - 1 do
        if self.FFunction.SlotAlign(LI) > LAlign then
          LAlign := self.FFunction.SlotAlign(LI);
        end;
      end;
      return LAlign;
    end;

    // FFrameReg: the ABI's frame register when a slot is aligned above the ABI's stack
    // alignment (the frame is realigned), else -1
    hidden method DoFrameRegister();
    begin
      if self.DoSlotAlign() > self.FAbi.StackAlign() then
        self.FFrameReg := self.DoPhysical(self.FAbi.FrameRegister());
      end;
    end;

    // The physical registers AInstr reads into AReads and writes into AWrites (both sized to
    // the arch's registers, cleared first)
    hidden method DoAccess(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; var AReads: BoolArray;
      var AWrites: BoolArray);
    var
      LOperand: ref MachineOperand;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      setlength(AReads, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(AWrites, self.FRegisters);
      for LI := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        AReads[LI] := false;
        AWrites[LI] := false;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to AInstr.OperandCount - 1 do
        LOperand := AInstr.OperandAt(LI);
        if LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.PhysicalReg then
          if (LI > 0) or X64OpReadsDest(AInstr.Op) then
            AReads[LOperand.Reg] := true;
          end;
          if (LI = 0) and X64OpWritesDest(AInstr.Op) then
            AWrites[LOperand.Reg] := true;
          end;
        end;
        if (LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.Memory) and (LOperand.Base = MemoryBase.Register) and
          not LOperand.BaseVirtual then
          AReads[LOperand.Reg] := true;
        end;
        if (LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.Memory) and (LOperand.Scale > 0) and
          not LOperand.IndexVirtual then
          AReads[LOperand.IndexReg] := true;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to AInstr.ImplicitUses.Count - 1 do
        AReads[AInstr.ImplicitUses[LI]] := true;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to AInstr.ImplicitDefs.Count - 1 do
        AWrites[AInstr.ImplicitDefs[LI]] := true;
      end;
    end;

    // Every block closed (see the header): one that falls through gets a jump to the next
    // block, an empty last block a nop
    hidden method DoCloseBlocks();
    var
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LJump: ref MachineInstr;
      LNode: int64;
      LCount: int64;
      LB: int64;
    begin
      for LB := 0 to self.FFunction.BlockCount - 1 do
        LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB);
        LCount := LBlock.InstrCount;
        if (LCount = 0) or not X64OpCloses(LBlock.InstrAt(LCount - 1).Op) then
          LNode := self.FFunction.Node;
          if LCount > 0 then
            LNode := LBlock.InstrAt(LCount - 1).Node;
          end;
          if LB + 1 < self.FFunction.BlockCount then
            LJump := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Jmp, 0, LNode);
            LJump.AddOperand(BlockOperand(LB + 1));
            LBlock.AddInstr(LJump);
          else
            if LCount = 0 then
              LBlock.AddInstr(ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Nop, 0, LNode));
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Each block's closing jumps, successors and predecessor count; raises for a jump
    // before a block's closing jumps
    hidden method DoCfg();
    var
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LOperand: ref MachineOperand;
      LTrail: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FBlockCount := self.FFunction.BlockCount;
      setlength(self.FSuccs, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FPredCount, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FTrail, self.FBlockCount);
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        self.FSuccs[LB] := ref Int64List();
        self.FPredCount[LB] := 0;
      end;
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB);
        LTrail := LBlock.InstrCount;
        while LTrail > 0 do
          if not DoIsJump(LBlock.InstrAt(LTrail - 1).Op) then
            leave;
          end;
          LTrail := LTrail - 1;
        end;
        self.FTrail[LB] := LTrail;
        for LK := 0 to LBlock.InstrCount - 1 do
          LInstr := LBlock.InstrAt(LK);
          if (LK < LTrail) and DoIsJump(LInstr.Op) then
            raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_INNER_JUMP + IntToStr(LB) + " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
          end;
          for LI := 0 to LInstr.OperandCount - 1 do
            LOperand := LInstr.OperandAt(LI);
            if (LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.BlockRef) and
              (self.FSuccs[LB].IndexOf(LOperand.Block) < 0) then
              self.FSuccs[LB].Add(LOperand.Block);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        for LK := 0 to self.FSuccs[LB].Count - 1 do
          self.FPredCount[self.FSuccs[LB][LK]] := self.FPredCount[self.FSuccs[LB][LK]] + 1;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The numbering (see the header): reverse postorder from the entry, then the blocks no
    // edge reaches in their order; each block's positions and each instruction's number
    hidden method DoNumber();
    var
      LSeen: BoolArray;
      LStack: ref Int64List;
      LNext: ref Int64List;
      LPost: ref Int64List;
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LTotal: int64;
      LTop: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LS: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LN: int64;
      LG: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LSeen, self.FBlockCount);
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        LSeen[LB] := false;
      end;
      // Depth first from the entry, each block's successors in order
      LStack := ref Int64List();
      LNext := ref Int64List();
      LPost := ref Int64List();
      LSeen[0] := true;
      LStack.Add(0);
      LNext.Add(0);
      while LStack.Count > 0 do
        LTop := LStack.Count - 1;
        LB := LStack[LTop];
        LK := LNext[LTop];
        if LK < self.FSuccs[LB].Count then
          LNext[LTop] := LK + 1;
          LS := self.FSuccs[LB][LK];
          if not LSeen[LS] then
            LSeen[LS] := true;
            LStack.Add(LS);
            LNext.Add(0);
          end;
        else
          LStack.RemoveLast();
          LNext.RemoveLast();
          LPost.Add(LB);
        end;
      end;
      for LN := LPost.Count - 1 downto 0 do
        self.FOrder.Add(LPost[LN]);
      end;
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        if not LSeen[LB] then
          self.FOrder.Add(LB);
        end;
      end;
      LTotal := 0;
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        LTotal := LTotal + self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB).InstrCount;
      end;
      setlength(self.FFirst, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FFrom, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FTo, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FInstrs, LTotal);
      setlength(self.FBlockOf, LTotal);
      LG := 0;
      for LN := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        LB := self.FOrder[LN];
        LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB);
        self.FFirst[LB] := LG;
        self.FFrom[LB] := 2 * LG;
        for LK := 0 to LBlock.InstrCount - 1 do
          self.FInstrs[LG] := LBlock.InstrAt(LK);
          self.FBlockOf[LG] := LB;
          LG := LG + 1;
        end;
        self.FTo[LB] := 2 * LG;
      end;
      self.FInstrCount := LG;
      setlength(self.FMovesBefore, LTotal);
      for LG := 0 to LTotal - 1 do
        self.FMovesBefore[LG] := nil;
      end;
      setlength(self.FMovesStart, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FMovesEnd, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FRetargetFrom, self.FBlockCount);
      setlength(self.FRetargetTo, self.FBlockCount);
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        self.FMovesStart[LB] := nil;
        self.FMovesEnd[LB] := nil;
        self.FRetargetFrom[LB] := ref Int64List();
        self.FRetargetTo[LB] := ref Int64List();
      end;
    end;

    // The bit of virtual register AVReg in its word
    hidden method DoMask(const AVReg: int64): uint64;
    begin
      return uint64(1) shl uint64(AVReg mod 64);
    end;

    // The virtual registers live into and out of each block (backward, to a fixed point
    // over the numbering's reverse), then the ones kept in their slot (see the header)
    hidden method DoLiveness();
    var
      LGen: BitWords;
      LKill: BitWords;
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LOut: uint64;
      LIn: uint64;
      LChanged: bool;
      LIndex: int64;
      LSize: int64;
      LV: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LN: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LW: int64;
      LBit: int64;
    begin
      self.FWords := (self.FFunction.VRegCount + 63) div 64;
      if self.FWords = 0 then
        self.FWords := 1;
      end;
      LSize := self.FBlockCount * self.FWords;
      setlength(LGen, LSize);
      setlength(LKill, LSize);
      setlength(self.FLiveIn, LSize);
      setlength(self.FLiveOut, LSize);
      for LI := 0 to LSize - 1 do
        LGen[LI] := 0;
        LKill[LI] := 0;
        self.FLiveIn[LI] := 0;
        self.FLiveOut[LI] := 0;
      end;
      // Per block: read before written (gen), written (kill)
      for LB := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB);
        for LK := 0 to LBlock.InstrCount - 1 do
          LInstr := LBlock.InstrAt(LK);
          for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
            LV := DoRefVReg(LInstr, LI);
            if (LV >= 0) and DoRefReads(LInstr, LI) then
              LIndex := LB * self.FWords + LV div 64;
              if (LKill[LIndex] & self.DoMask(LV)) = 0 then
                LGen[LIndex] := LGen[LIndex] | self.DoMask(LV);
              end;
            end;
          end;
          for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
            LV := DoRefVReg(LInstr, LI);
            if (LV >= 0) and DoRefWrites(LInstr, LI) then
              LIndex := LB * self.FWords + LV div 64;
              LKill[LIndex] := LKill[LIndex] | self.DoMask(LV);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LChanged := true;
      while LChanged do
        LChanged := false;
        for LN := self.FOrder.Count - 1 downto 0 do
          LB := self.FOrder[LN];
          for LW := 0 to self.FWords - 1 do
            LOut := 0;
            for LK := 0 to self.FSuccs[LB].Count - 1 do
              LOut := LOut | self.FLiveIn[self.FSuccs[LB][LK] * self.FWords + LW];
            end;
            LIndex := LB * self.FWords + LW;
            self.FLiveOut[LIndex] := LOut;
            LIn := LGen[LIndex] | (LOut & (LKill[LIndex] xor 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFu));
            if LIn <> self.FLiveIn[LIndex] then
              self.FLiveIn[LIndex] := LIn;
              LChanged := true;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      // Live into a block no edge reaches (never the entry): kept in the slot
      setlength(self.FResident, self.FFunction.VRegCount);
      for LV := 0 to self.FFunction.VRegCount - 1 do
        self.FResident[LV] := false;
      end;
      for LB := 1 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        if self.FPredCount[LB] = 0 then
          for LW := 0 to self.FWords - 1 do
            LIn := self.FLiveIn[LB * self.FWords + LW];
            if LIn <> 0 then
              for LBit := 0 to 63 do
                if (LIn & (uint64(1) shl uint64(LBit))) <> 0 then
                  self.FResident[LW * 64 + LBit] := true;
                end;
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The fixed intervals (see the header), by a backward scan of each block in numbering
    // order (so each register's ranges come out ascending), the registers live into the
    // entry and those selection writes; raises for a register live into another block
    hidden method DoFixed();
    var
      LLiveEnd: Int64Array;
      LReads: BoolArray;
      LWrites: BoolArray;
      LRegs: ref Int64List;
      LFroms: ref Int64List;
      LTos: ref Int64List;
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LB: int64;
      LN: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LG: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      setlength(self.FFixedFroms, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FFixedTos, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FFixedCursor, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FEntryLive, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(self.FFixedWritten, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(LLiveEnd, self.FRegisters);
      for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        self.FFixedFroms[LR] := ref Int64List();
        self.FFixedTos[LR] := ref Int64List();
        self.FFixedCursor[LR] := 0;
        self.FEntryLive[LR] := false;
        self.FFixedWritten[LR] := false;
      end;
      for LN := 0 to self.FOrder.Count - 1 do
        LB := self.FOrder[LN];
        LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LB);
        for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
          LLiveEnd[LR] := -1;
        end;
        // The block's ranges, found backward (descending), put in ascending after
        LRegs := ref Int64List();
        LFroms := ref Int64List();
        LTos := ref Int64List();
        for LK := LBlock.InstrCount - 1 downto 0 do
          LG := self.FFirst[LB] + LK;
          self.DoAccess(LBlock.InstrAt(LK), LReads, LWrites);
          for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
            if LR = self.FStack then
              skip;
            end;
            if LWrites[LR] then
              self.FFixedWritten[LR] := true;
              LRegs.Add(LR);
              LFroms.Add(2 * LG + 1);
              if LLiveEnd[LR] >= 0 then
                LTos.Add(LLiveEnd[LR]);
                LLiveEnd[LR] := -1;
              else
                LTos.Add(2 * LG + 2);
              end;
            end;
            if LReads[LR] and (LLiveEnd[LR] < 0) then
              LLiveEnd[LR] := 2 * LG + 1;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
          if (LR <> self.FStack) and (LLiveEnd[LR] >= 0) then
            if LB <> 0 then
              raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_LIVE_IN + IntToStr(LB) + ": " +
                self.FRegisterTable.Text(LR));
            end;
            self.FEntryLive[LR] := true;
            LRegs.Add(LR);
            LFroms.Add(self.FFrom[LB]);
            LTos.Add(LLiveEnd[LR]);
          end;
        end;
        for LI := LRegs.Count - 1 downto 0 do
          self.FFixedFroms[LRegs[LI]].Add(LFroms[LI]);
          self.FFixedTos[LRegs[LI]].Add(LTos[LI]);
        end;
      end;
      for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        self.FSavedNow[LR] := self.FIsCallee[LR] and self.FFixedWritten[LR];
      end;
    end;

    // AInterval added to the intervals; returns its id
    hidden method DoAddInterval(const AInterval: ref LiveInterval): int64;
    begin
      if self.FIntervalCount = len(self.FIntervals) then
        setlength(self.FIntervals, self.FIntervalCount * 2 + 64);
      end;
      self.FIntervals[self.FIntervalCount] := AInterval;
      self.FIntervalCount := self.FIntervalCount + 1;
      return self.FIntervalCount - 1;
    end;

    // Virtual register AVReg's root interval, made the first time
    hidden method DoRootOf(const AVReg: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FRootOf[AVReg] < 0 then
        self.FRootOf[AVReg] := self.DoAddInterval(ref LiveInterval(AVReg,
          self.FFunction.VRegClass(AVReg) = RegClass.Vector));
      end;
      return self.FRootOf[AVReg];
    end;

    // [AFrom, ATo) added to interval AId while it is built (backward: no range of it starts
    // before AFrom's block, so the range merges with its earliest one or comes before it)
    hidden method DoAddRange(const AId: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64);
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LLast: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LLast := LInterval.Froms.Count - 1;
      if (LLast < 0) or (ATo < LInterval.Froms[LLast]) then
        LInterval.Froms.Add(AFrom);
        LInterval.Tos.Add(ATo);
        return;
      end;
      if AFrom < LInterval.Froms[LLast] then
        LInterval.Froms[LLast] := AFrom;
      end;
      if ATo > LInterval.Tos[LLast] then
        LInterval.Tos[LLast] := ATo;
      end;
    end;

    // A use of interval AId at APos while it is built (positions come descending)
    hidden method DoAddUse(const AId: int64; const APos: int64);
    var
      LUses: ref Int64List;
    begin
      LUses := self.FIntervals[AId].Uses;
      if (LUses.Count = 0) or (LUses[LUses.Count - 1] <> APos) then
        LUses.Add(APos);
      end;
    end;

    // A write of interval AId at APos while it is built: its earliest range (the block's,
    // which holds APos) starts there, or a write nothing reads holds APos alone
    hidden method DoDefine(const AId: int64; const APos: int64);
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LLast: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LLast := LInterval.Froms.Count - 1;
      if (LLast >= 0) and (LInterval.Froms[LLast] <= APos) then
        LInterval.Froms[LLast] := APos;
      else
        LInterval.Froms.Add(APos);
        LInterval.Tos.Add(APos + 1);
      end;
      self.DoAddUse(AId, APos);
    end;

    // The hints a copy AInstr (number AG) gives: a register copied into a virtual one, a
    // virtual one copied into a register, a virtual one copied from another and the other
    // way round: the source told where its copy goes (the first copy found, scanning
    // backward, holds); every copy into a virtual register counted (FCopiesIn)
    hidden method DoHints(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const AG: int64);
    var
      LDest: ref MachineOperand;
      LSource: ref MachineOperand;
      LV: int64;
    begin
      if ((AInstr.Op <> X64Op.Mov) and (AInstr.Op <> X64Op.MovSS) and
        (AInstr.Op <> X64Op.MovSD)) or (AInstr.OperandCount <> 2) then
        return;
      end;
      LDest := AInstr.OperandAt(0);
      LSource := AInstr.OperandAt(1);
      if (LDest.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg) and not self.FResident[LDest.Reg] then
        LV := LDest.Reg;
        self.FCopiesIn[LV] := self.FCopiesIn[LV] + 1;
        if (LSource.Kind = OperandKind.PhysicalReg) and (self.FHintReg[LV] < 0) then
          self.FHintReg[LV] := LSource.Reg;
        end;
        if (LSource.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg) and (self.FHintVReg[LV] < 0) then
          self.FHintVReg[LV] := LSource.Reg;
          self.FHintAt[LV] := 2 * AG;
        end;
        if (LSource.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg) and not self.FResident[LSource.Reg] and
          (self.FHintOut[LSource.Reg] < 0) then
          self.FHintOut[LSource.Reg] := LV;
          self.FHintOutAt[LSource.Reg] := 2 * AG + 1;
        end;
      end;
      if (LDest.Kind = OperandKind.PhysicalReg) and (LSource.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg) and
        not self.FResident[LSource.Reg] then
        LV := LSource.Reg;
        if self.FHintReg[LV] < 0 then
          self.FHintReg[LV] := LDest.Reg;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Each virtual register's root interval (the ones kept in their slot have none), by a
    // backward walk of the numbering: a value live out of a block holds the whole block, a
    // write starts its range, a read reaches back to the block's start; then each interval
    // put ascending and into the walk
    hidden method DoIntervals();
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LWord: uint64;
      LCount: int64;
      LB: int64;
      LN: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LG: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LV: int64;
      LW: int64;
      LBit: int64;
    begin
      LCount := self.FFunction.VRegCount;
      setlength(self.FRootOf, LCount);
      setlength(self.FPartsOf, LCount);
      setlength(self.FHintReg, LCount);
      setlength(self.FHintVReg, LCount);
      setlength(self.FHintAt, LCount);
      setlength(self.FHintOut, LCount);
      setlength(self.FHintOutAt, LCount);
      setlength(self.FCopiesIn, LCount);
      setlength(self.FSlotOf, LCount);
      for LV := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        self.FRootOf[LV] := -1;
        self.FPartsOf[LV] := ref Int64List();
        self.FHintReg[LV] := -1;
        self.FHintVReg[LV] := -1;
        self.FHintAt[LV] := -1;
        self.FHintOut[LV] := -1;
        self.FHintOutAt[LV] := -1;
        self.FCopiesIn[LV] := 0;
        self.FSlotOf[LV] := -1;
      end;
      for LN := self.FOrder.Count - 1 downto 0 do
        LB := self.FOrder[LN];
        for LW := 0 to self.FWords - 1 do
          LWord := self.FLiveOut[LB * self.FWords + LW];
          if LWord <> 0 then
            for LBit := 0 to 63 do
              if (LWord & (uint64(1) shl uint64(LBit))) <> 0 then
                LV := LW * 64 + LBit;
                if not self.FResident[LV] then
                  self.DoAddRange(self.DoRootOf(LV), self.FFrom[LB], self.FTo[LB]);
                end;
              end;
            end;
          end;
        end;
        for LK := (self.FTo[LB] - self.FFrom[LB]) div 2 - 1 downto 0 do
          LG := self.FFirst[LB] + LK;
          LInstr := self.FInstrs[LG];
          // Its writes first, then its reads (backward)
          for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
            LV := DoRefVReg(LInstr, LI);
            if (LV >= 0) and not self.FResident[LV] and DoRefWrites(LInstr, LI) then
              self.DoDefine(self.DoRootOf(LV), 2 * LG + 1);
            end;
          end;
          for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
            LV := DoRefVReg(LInstr, LI);
            if (LV >= 0) and not self.FResident[LV] and DoRefReads(LInstr, LI) then
              self.DoAddRange(self.DoRootOf(LV), self.FFrom[LB], 2 * LG + 1);
              self.DoAddUse(self.DoRootOf(LV), 2 * LG);
            end;
          end;
          self.DoHints(LInstr, LG);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FIntervalCount - 1 do
        LInterval := self.FIntervals[LI];
        LInterval.Froms := DoReversed(LInterval.Froms);
        LInterval.Tos := DoReversed(LInterval.Tos);
        LInterval.Uses := DoReversed(LInterval.Uses);
      end;
      for LV := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if self.FRootOf[LV] >= 0 then
          self.FPartsOf[LV].Add(self.FRootOf[LV]);
          self.DoPush(self.FRootOf[LV]);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The pieces of the virtual registers kept in their slot (see the header): per
    // instruction naming one, an interval over its read and / or write position
    hidden method DoPieces();
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LPiece: ref LiveInterval;
      LNamed: bool;
      LRead: bool;
      LWrite: bool;
      LId: int64;
      LG: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
      LV: int64;
    begin
      for LG := 0 to self.FInstrCount - 1 do
        LInstr := self.FInstrs[LG];
        for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
          LV := DoRefVReg(LInstr, LI);
          if (LV < 0) or not self.FResident[LV] then
            skip;
          end;
          // Once per instruction
          LNamed := false;
          for LJ := 0 to LI - 1 do
            if DoRefVReg(LInstr, LJ) = LV then
              LNamed := true;
            end;
          end;
          if LNamed then
            skip;
          end;
          LRead := false;
          LWrite := false;
          for LJ := LI to DoRefCount(LInstr) - 1 do
            if DoRefVReg(LInstr, LJ) = LV then
              if DoRefReads(LInstr, LJ) then
                LRead := true;
              end;
              if DoRefWrites(LInstr, LJ) then
                LWrite := true;
              end;
            end;
          end;
          LPiece := ref LiveInterval(LV, self.FFunction.VRegClass(LV) = RegClass.Vector);
          if LRead then
            LPiece.Froms.Add(2 * LG);
            LPiece.Uses.Add(2 * LG);
          else
            LPiece.Froms.Add(2 * LG + 1);
          end;
          if LWrite then
            LPiece.Tos.Add(2 * LG + 2);
            LPiece.Uses.Add(2 * LG + 1);
          else
            LPiece.Tos.Add(2 * LG + 1);
          end;
          LId := self.DoAddInterval(LPiece);
          self.FPartsOf[LV].Add(LId);
          self.DoSlotOf(LV);
          self.DoPush(LId);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Virtual register AVReg's spill slot, made the first time
    hidden method DoSlotOf(const AVReg: int64): int64;
    begin
      if self.FSlotOf[AVReg] < 0 then
        self.FSlotOf[AVReg] := self.FFunction.AddSlot(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES,
          ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES);
      end;
      return self.FSlotOf[AVReg];
    end;

    // True when interval AA is taken before AB: the earlier start, then the lower id
    hidden method DoBefore(const AA: int64; const AB: int64): bool;
    var
      LStartA: int64;
      LStartB: int64;
    begin
      LStartA := self.FIntervals[AA].Start();
      LStartB := self.FIntervals[AB].Start();
      if LStartA <> LStartB then
        return LStartA < LStartB;
      end;
      return AA < AB;
    end;

    // Interval AId into the walk's heap; raises for one starting before the walk's position
    hidden method DoPush(const AId: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
      LParent: int64;
      LSwap: int64;
    begin
      if self.FIntervals[AId].Start() < self.FWalkPos then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_ORDER + self.DoVRegText(self.FIntervals[AId].VReg) + " in " +
          self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      self.FHeap.Add(AId);
      LI := self.FHeap.Count - 1;
      while LI > 0 do
        LParent := (LI - 1) div 2;
        if not self.DoBefore(self.FHeap[LI], self.FHeap[LParent]) then
          leave;
        end;
        LSwap := self.FHeap[LI];
        self.FHeap[LI] := self.FHeap[LParent];
        self.FHeap[LParent] := LSwap;
        LI := LParent;
      end;
    end;

    // The heap's first interval, taken off it
    hidden method DoPop(): int64;
    var
      LTop: int64;
      LLast: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LLeft: int64;
      LRight: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LSwap: int64;
    begin
      LTop := self.FHeap[0];
      LLast := self.FHeap.RemoveLast();
      if self.FHeap.Count = 0 then
        return LTop;
      end;
      self.FHeap[0] := LLast;
      LI := 0;
      while true do
        LLeft := 2 * LI + 1;
        LRight := LLeft + 1;
        LFirst := LI;
        if (LLeft < self.FHeap.Count) and self.DoBefore(self.FHeap[LLeft], self.FHeap[LFirst]) then
          LFirst := LLeft;
        end;
        if (LRight < self.FHeap.Count) and
          self.DoBefore(self.FHeap[LRight], self.FHeap[LFirst]) then
          LFirst := LRight;
        end;
        if LFirst = LI then
          leave;
        end;
        LSwap := self.FHeap[LI];
        self.FHeap[LI] := self.FHeap[LFirst];
        self.FHeap[LFirst] := LSwap;
        LI := LFirst;
      end;
      return LTop;
    end;

    // Interval AId split at AAt (strictly inside it): it keeps what lies before, a new part
    // (no place yet, after it in its virtual register's parts) takes the rest; returns the
    // new part's id
    hidden method DoSplit(const AId: int64; const AAt: int64): int64;
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LChild: ref LiveInterval;
      LFroms: ref Int64List;
      LTos: ref Int64List;
      LUses: ref Int64List;
      LChildId: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      if (AAt <= LInterval.Start()) or (AAt >= LInterval.Finish()) then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_SPLIT + self.DoVRegText(LInterval.VReg) + " at " +
          IntToStr(AAt) + " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      LChild := ref LiveInterval(LInterval.VReg, LInterval.IsVector);
      LFroms := ref Int64List();
      LTos := ref Int64List();
      LUses := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to LInterval.Froms.Count - 1 do
        LFrom := LInterval.Froms[LI];
        LTo := LInterval.Tos[LI];
        if LTo <= AAt then
          LFroms.Add(LFrom);
          LTos.Add(LTo);
        else
          if LFrom >= AAt then
            LChild.Froms.Add(LFrom);
            LChild.Tos.Add(LTo);
          else
            LFroms.Add(LFrom);
            LTos.Add(AAt);
            LChild.Froms.Add(AAt);
            LChild.Tos.Add(LTo);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LInterval.Uses.Count - 1 do
        if LInterval.Uses[LI] < AAt then
          LUses.Add(LInterval.Uses[LI]);
        else
          LChild.Uses.Add(LInterval.Uses[LI]);
        end;
      end;
      LInterval.Froms := LFroms;
      LInterval.Tos := LTos;
      LInterval.Uses := LUses;
      LChildId := self.DoAddInterval(LChild);
      DoInsertAfter(self.FPartsOf[LInterval.VReg], AId, LChildId);
      return LChildId;
    end;

    // APos (a split position) moved off a block's closing jumps: one between them becomes
    // the first's (see the header)
    hidden method DoNormalize(const APos: int64): int64;
    var
      LG: int64;
      LB: int64;
    begin
      if APos >= 2 * self.FInstrCount then
        return APos;
      end;
      LG := APos div 2;
      LB := self.FBlockOf[LG];
      if LG - self.FFirst[LB] > self.FTrail[LB] then
        return 2 * (self.FFirst[LB] + self.FTrail[LB]);
      end;
      return APos;
    end;

    // Where virtual register AVReg is at APos: a register, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT, or
    // ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE (not live there, or that part not placed)
    hidden method DoLocation(const AVReg: int64; const APos: int64): int64;
    var
      LParts: ref Int64List;
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LParts := self.FPartsOf[AVReg];
      for LI := 0 to LParts.Count - 1 do
        LInterval := self.FIntervals[LParts[LI]];
        if LInterval.Start() > APos then
          leave;
        end;
        if LInterval.Covers(APos) then
          if LInterval.InSlot then
            return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT;
          end;
          if LInterval.Reg >= 0 then
            return LInterval.Reg;
          end;
          return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE;
        end;
      end;
      return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE;
    end;

    // The register virtual register AHint (a copy hint; -1: none) is in at APos, added to
    // AList when it is known; one not placed yet gives its physical hint, else passes the
    // hint on along its own copy, the way AOut says (true: the copy it goes into,
    // FHintOut; false: the copy it comes from, FHintVReg), up to ADAM_X64_ALLOC_HINT_HOPS
    // copies; one in its slot ends the chain
    hidden method DoAddHintPlace(const AList: ref Int64List; const AHint: int64;
      const APos: int64; const AOut: bool);
    var
      LHint: int64;
      LPos: int64;
      LPlace: int64;
      LHop: int64;
    begin
      LHint := AHint;
      LPos := APos;
      LHop := 0;
      while (LHint >= 0) and (LHop < ADAM_X64_ALLOC_HINT_HOPS) do
        LPlace := self.DoLocation(LHint, LPos);
        if LPlace >= 0 then
          AList.Add(LPlace);
          return;
        end;
        if LPlace <> ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE then
          return;
        end;
        // Not placed yet but bound for a register (a copy into an argument's, say): there
        if self.FHintReg[LHint] >= 0 then
          AList.Add(self.FHintReg[LHint]);
          return;
        end;
        if AOut then
          LPos := self.FHintOutAt[LHint];
          LHint := self.FHintOut[LHint];
        else
          LPos := self.FHintAt[LHint];
          LHint := self.FHintVReg[LHint];
        end;
        LHop := LHop + 1;
      end;
    end;

    // The registers interval AId would best take, best first: the one its value is in
    // just before it, its physical hint, then where the value copied into it is (at that
    // copy) and where the value it is copied into is (at that copy). A join's value (more
    // than one copy writes it: a phi with its edges) takes the copy out first: its copies in
    // come from registers that differ edge by edge, its one copy out is coalesced whole
    hidden method DoHintsOf(const AId: int64): ref Int64List;
    var
      LHints: ref Int64List;
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LPlace: int64;
      LV: int64;
    begin
      LHints := ref Int64List();
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LV := LInterval.VReg;
      LPlace := self.DoLocation(LV, LInterval.Start() - 1);
      if LPlace >= 0 then
        LHints.Add(LPlace);
      end;
      if self.FHintReg[LV] >= 0 then
        LHints.Add(self.FHintReg[LV]);
      end;
      if self.FCopiesIn[LV] > 1 then
        self.DoAddHintPlace(LHints, self.FHintOut[LV], self.FHintOutAt[LV], true);
        self.DoAddHintPlace(LHints, self.FHintVReg[LV], self.FHintAt[LV], false);
      else
        self.DoAddHintPlace(LHints, self.FHintVReg[LV], self.FHintAt[LV], false);
        self.DoAddHintPlace(LHints, self.FHintOut[LV], self.FHintOutAt[LV], true);
      end;
      return LHints;
    end;

    // The first position register AReg's fixed intervals meet interval AInterval (the
    // current one) at; ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER for none
    hidden method DoFixedMeet(const AReg: int64; const AInterval: ref LiveInterval): int64;
    var
      LTos: ref Int64List;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LTos := self.FFixedTos[AReg];
      LAt := self.FFixedCursor[AReg];
      while (LAt < LTos.Count) and (LTos[LAt] <= self.FWalkPos) do
        LAt := LAt + 1;
      end;
      self.FFixedCursor[AReg] := LAt;
      return DoMeet(self.FFixedFroms[AReg], LTos, LAt, AInterval.Froms, AInterval.Tos);
    end;

    // The active and inactive sets moved to APos: an interval ended drops out, one in a hole
    // there is inactive, one holding it active
    hidden method DoAdvance(const APos: int64);
    var
      LActive: ref Int64List;
      LInactive: ref Int64List;
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LActive := ref Int64List();
      LInactive := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to self.FActive.Count - 1 do
        LInterval := self.FIntervals[self.FActive[LI]];
        if LInterval.Finish() > APos then
          if LInterval.Covers(APos) then
            LActive.Add(self.FActive[LI]);
          else
            LInactive.Add(self.FActive[LI]);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FInactive.Count - 1 do
        LInterval := self.FIntervals[self.FInactive[LI]];
        if LInterval.Finish() > APos then
          if LInterval.Covers(APos) then
            LActive.Add(self.FInactive[LI]);
          else
            LInactive.Add(self.FInactive[LI]);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      self.FActive := LActive;
      self.FInactive := LInactive;
    end;

    // Interval AId out of the active and inactive sets
    hidden method DoDrop(const AId: int64);
    var
      LActive: ref Int64List;
      LInactive: ref Int64List;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LActive := ref Int64List();
      LInactive := ref Int64List();
      for LI := 0 to self.FActive.Count - 1 do
        if self.FActive[LI] <> AId then
          LActive.Add(self.FActive[LI]);
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FInactive.Count - 1 do
        if self.FInactive[LI] <> AId then
          LInactive.Add(self.FInactive[LI]);
        end;
      end;
      self.FActive := LActive;
      self.FInactive := LInactive;
    end;

    // Register AReg given to interval AId (a callee-saved one is saved from then on)
    hidden method DoGive(const AId: int64; const AReg: int64);
    begin
      self.FIntervals[AId].Reg := AReg;
      if self.FIsCallee[AReg] then
        self.FSavedNow[AReg] := true;
      end;
    end;

    // Interval AId (no place) kept in its slot up to its next use, the rest back into the
    // walk; all of it in the slot when it has no use
    hidden method DoPark(const AId: int64);
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LUse: int64;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LUse := LInterval.UseFrom(LInterval.Start());
      if LUse = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER then
        LInterval.InSlot := true;
        self.DoSlotOf(LInterval.VReg);
        return;
      end;
      LAt := self.DoNormalize(DoEven(LUse));
      if LAt <= LInterval.Start() then
        self.DoPush(AId);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoPush(self.DoSplit(AId, LAt));
      LInterval.InSlot := true;
      self.DoSlotOf(LInterval.VReg);
    end;

    // Interval AId (holding a register) loses it from AAt on: split there (all of it when
    // AAt is at or before its start), the part from AAt parked (DoPark)
    hidden method DoEvict(const AId: int64; const AAt: int64);
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      if AAt >= LInterval.Finish() then
        return;
      end;
      if AAt <= LInterval.Start() then
        LInterval.Reg := -1;
        self.DoDrop(AId);
        self.DoPark(AId);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoPark(self.DoSplit(AId, AAt));
    end;

    // The first of ACands (by preference, see the header) free for all of an interval
    // ending at AEnd (AFree: where each register stops being free); -1 for none. A fresh
    // callee-saved register only when AAllowFresh
    hidden method DoWhole(const ACands: ref Int64List; const AFree: Int64Array;
      const AEnd: int64; const AAllowFresh: bool): int64;
    var
      LPass: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LPass := 0 to 2 do
        for LI := 0 to ACands.Count - 1 do
          LR := ACands[LI];
          if AFree[LR] >= AEnd then
            if (LPass = 0) and self.FIsVolatile[LR] then
              return LR;
            end;
            if (LPass = 1) and self.FIsCallee[LR] and self.FSavedNow[LR] then
              return LR;
            end;
            if (LPass = 2) and AAllowFresh and self.FIsCallee[LR] and not self.FSavedNow[LR] then
              return LR;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return -1;
    end;

    // The register of ACands free longest past APos for part of an interval ending at AEnd
    // (a split before it must fall after APos); -1 for none. A fresh callee-saved register
    // only when AAllowFresh
    hidden method DoLongest(const ACands: ref Int64List; const AFree: Int64Array;
      const APos: int64; const AEnd: int64; const AAllowFresh: bool): int64;
    var
      LBest: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LBest := -1;
      for LI := 0 to ACands.Count - 1 do
        LR := ACands[LI];
        if self.FIsCallee[LR] and not self.FSavedNow[LR] and not AAllowFresh then
          skip;
        end;
        if (AFree[LR] < AEnd) and (self.DoNormalize(DoEven(AFree[LR])) > APos) then
          if (LBest < 0) or (AFree[LR] > AFree[LBest]) then
            LBest := LR;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      return LBest;
    end;

    // The candidates of interval AInterval's class
    hidden method DoCandidatesOf(const AInterval: ref LiveInterval): ref Int64List;
    begin
      if AInterval.IsVector then
        return self.FVector;
      end;
      return self.FGeneral;
    end;

    // Interval AId given a register free for it (see the header), or for a first part of
    // it (the rest split off into the walk); false when none is free at its start
    hidden method DoTryFree(const AId: int64): bool;
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LOther: ref LiveInterval;
      LCands: ref Int64List;
      LFree: Int64Array;
      LAllowFresh: bool;
      LHints: ref Int64List;
      LPos: int64;
      LEnd: int64;
      LHint: int64;
      LPick: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LPos := LInterval.Start();
      LEnd := LInterval.Finish();
      LCands := self.DoCandidatesOf(LInterval);
      setlength(LFree, self.FRegisters);
      for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        LFree[LR] := ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FActive.Count - 1 do
        LFree[self.FIntervals[self.FActive[LI]].Reg] := 0;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FInactive.Count - 1 do
        LOther := self.FIntervals[self.FInactive[LI]];
        if LFree[LOther.Reg] > LPos then
          LAt := DoMeet(LOther.Froms, LOther.Tos, 0, LInterval.Froms, LInterval.Tos);
          if LAt < LFree[LOther.Reg] then
            LFree[LOther.Reg] := LAt;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCands.Count - 1 do
        LR := LCands[LI];
        LAt := self.DoFixedMeet(LR, LInterval);
        if LAt < LFree[LR] then
          LFree[LR] := LAt;
        end;
      end;
      LAllowFresh := LInterval.Uses.Count >= ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SAVE_USES;
      // The first hint that is a candidate and free for the whole interval
      LHints := self.DoHintsOf(AId);
      for LI := 0 to LHints.Count - 1 do
        LHint := LHints[LI];
        if (LCands.IndexOf(LHint) >= 0) and (LFree[LHint] >= LEnd) then
          self.DoGive(AId, LHint);
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      LPick := self.DoWhole(LCands, LFree, LEnd, LAllowFresh);
      if LPick < 0 then
        LPick := self.DoLongest(LCands, LFree, LPos, LEnd, LAllowFresh);
      end;
      if (LPick < 0) and not LAllowFresh then
        // Nothing else: a fresh callee-saved register after all
        LPick := self.DoWhole(LCands, LFree, LEnd, true);
        if LPick < 0 then
          LPick := self.DoLongest(LCands, LFree, LPos, LEnd, true);
        end;
      end;
      if LPick < 0 then
        return false;
      end;
      self.DoGive(AId, LPick);
      if LFree[LPick] < LEnd then
        self.DoPush(self.DoSplit(AId, self.DoNormalize(DoEven(LFree[LPick]))));
      end;
      return true;
    end;

    // Interval AId given the register whose holders are used furthest ahead, taken from
    // them, or kept in its slot up to its first use when every register is needed sooner
    // (see the header); raises when an instruction needs more registers than there are
    hidden method DoBlocked(const AId: int64);
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LOther: ref LiveInterval;
      LCands: ref Int64List;
      LHolders: ref Int64List;
      LUse: Int64Array;
      LBlockAt: Int64Array;
      LPos: int64;
      LInstrPos: int64;
      LFirstUse: int64;
      LPick: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      LPos := LInterval.Start();
      LInstrPos := DoEven(LPos);
      LFirstUse := LInterval.UseFrom(LPos);
      LCands := self.DoCandidatesOf(LInterval);
      setlength(LUse, self.FRegisters);
      setlength(LBlockAt, self.FRegisters);
      for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        LUse[LR] := ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
        LBlockAt[LR] := ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LCands.Count - 1 do
        LR := LCands[LI];
        LBlockAt[LR] := self.DoFixedMeet(LR, LInterval);
        LUse[LR] := LBlockAt[LR];
      end;
      // A holder's next use counts from the current's instruction: one it reads there keeps
      // its register through it
      for LI := 0 to self.FActive.Count - 1 do
        LOther := self.FIntervals[self.FActive[LI]];
        LAt := LOther.UseFrom(LInstrPos);
        if LAt < LUse[LOther.Reg] then
          LUse[LOther.Reg] := LAt;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FInactive.Count - 1 do
        LOther := self.FIntervals[self.FInactive[LI]];
        if DoMeet(LOther.Froms, LOther.Tos, 0, LInterval.Froms, LInterval.Tos) <
          ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER then
          LAt := LOther.UseFrom(LInstrPos);
          if LAt < LUse[LOther.Reg] then
            LUse[LOther.Reg] := LAt;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LPick := -1;
      for LI := 0 to LCands.Count - 1 do
        LR := LCands[LI];
        if (LBlockAt[LR] = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER) or
          (self.DoNormalize(DoEven(LBlockAt[LR])) > LPos) then
          if (LPick < 0) or (LUse[LR] > LUse[LPick]) then
            LPick := LR;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if (LPick < 0) or (LUse[LPick] <= LFirstUse) then
        // Every register is needed no later than the current, or fixed through its start
        // (a call's volatile set): it waits in its slot
        LAt := self.DoNormalize(DoEven(LFirstUse));
        if LAt <= LPos then
          raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_FREE + self.DoVRegText(LInterval.VReg) + " at " +
            IntToStr(LPos) + " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
        end;
        self.DoPush(self.DoSplit(AId, LAt));
        LInterval.InSlot := true;
        self.DoSlotOf(LInterval.VReg);
        return;
      end;
      self.DoGive(AId, LPick);
      if LBlockAt[LPick] < LInterval.Finish() then
        self.DoPush(self.DoSplit(AId, self.DoNormalize(DoEven(LBlockAt[LPick]))));
      end;
      // The holders: an active one gives the register up from the current's instruction, an
      // inactive one meeting the current from where it is live again
      LHolders := self.FActive;
      for LI := 0 to LHolders.Count - 1 do
        LOther := self.FIntervals[LHolders[LI]];
        if (LHolders[LI] <> AId) and (LOther.Reg = LPick) then
          self.DoEvict(LHolders[LI], LInstrPos);
        end;
      end;
      LHolders := self.FInactive;
      for LI := 0 to LHolders.Count - 1 do
        LOther := self.FIntervals[LHolders[LI]];
        if (LOther.Reg = LPick) and
          (DoMeet(LOther.Froms, LOther.Tos, 0, LInterval.Froms, LInterval.Tos) <
          ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER) then
          self.DoEvict(LHolders[LI], DoEven(LOther.RangeFrom(LPos)));
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The walk (see the header): each interval by start, given a register or a slot
    hidden method DoWalk();
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
      LLimit: int64;
      LId: int64;
      LPos: int64;
    begin
      LLimit := ADAM_X64_ALLOC_WALK_FACTOR * (self.FInstrCount + self.FFunction.VRegCount + 1);
      while self.FHeap.Count > 0 do
        self.FSteps := self.FSteps + 1;
        if self.FSteps > LLimit then
          raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_WALK + self.FFunction.Symbol);
        end;
        LId := self.DoPop();
        LInterval := self.FIntervals[LId];
        LPos := LInterval.Start();
        self.FWalkPos := LPos;
        self.DoAdvance(LPos);
        if LInterval.UseFrom(LPos) = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NEVER then
          LInterval.InSlot := true;
          self.DoSlotOf(LInterval.VReg);
          skip;
        end;
        if not self.DoTryFree(LId) then
          self.DoBlocked(LId);
        end;
        if LInterval.Reg >= 0 then
          self.FActive.Add(LId);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // AMoves (one edge's or one position's, each to a distinct place) as one parallel move,
    // in order (see the header): the stores, the register moves each after every move
    // reading its destination (a cycle broken by sending one value to its slot), the reloads
    hidden method DoSequence(const AMoves: ref MoveList): ref MoveList;
    var
      LOrdered: ref MoveList;
      LReloads: ref MoveList;
      LDone: BoolArray;
      LFound: bool;
      LBlocked: bool;
      LCount: int64;
      LLeft: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LJ: int64;
    begin
      LOrdered := ref MoveList();
      LReloads := ref MoveList();
      LCount := AMoves.Count();
      setlength(LDone, LCount);
      LLeft := 0;
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LDone[LI] := false;
        if AMoves.Tos[LI] = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT then
          self.DoSlotOf(AMoves.VRegs[LI]);
          LOrdered.Add(AMoves.VRegs[LI], AMoves.Froms[LI], AMoves.Tos[LI]);
          LDone[LI] := true;
        else
          if AMoves.Froms[LI] = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT then
            LReloads.Add(AMoves.VRegs[LI], AMoves.Froms[LI], AMoves.Tos[LI]);
            LDone[LI] := true;
          else
            LLeft := LLeft + 1;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      while LLeft > 0 do
        LFound := false;
        for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
          if LDone[LI] then
            skip;
          end;
          LBlocked := false;
          for LJ := 0 to LCount - 1 do
            if (LJ <> LI) and not LDone[LJ] and (AMoves.Froms[LJ] = AMoves.Tos[LI]) then
              LBlocked := true;
              leave;
            end;
          end;
          if not LBlocked then
            LOrdered.Add(AMoves.VRegs[LI], AMoves.Froms[LI], AMoves.Tos[LI]);
            LDone[LI] := true;
            LLeft := LLeft - 1;
            LFound := true;
            leave;
          end;
        end;
        if not LFound then
          // Every move left is in a cycle: the value in the first one's destination goes to
          // its slot and comes back last
          LI := 0;
          while LDone[LI] do
            LI := LI + 1;
          end;
          for LJ := 0 to LCount - 1 do
            if not LDone[LJ] and (AMoves.Froms[LJ] = AMoves.Tos[LI]) then
              self.DoSlotOf(AMoves.VRegs[LJ]);
              LOrdered.Add(AMoves.VRegs[LJ], AMoves.Froms[LJ], ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT);
              LReloads.Add(AMoves.VRegs[LJ], ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT, AMoves.Tos[LJ]);
              LDone[LJ] := true;
              LLeft := LLeft - 1;
              leave;
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to LReloads.Count() - 1 do
        LOrdered.Add(LReloads.VRegs[LI], LReloads.Froms[LI], LReloads.Tos[LI]);
      end;
      return LOrdered;
    end;

    // Where interval AId is (it has a place after the walk); raises when it has none
    hidden method DoPartPlace(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LInterval: ref LiveInterval;
    begin
      LInterval := self.FIntervals[AId];
      if LInterval.InSlot then
        return ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT;
      end;
      if LInterval.Reg < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_PLACE + self.DoVRegText(LInterval.VReg) + " at " +
          IntToStr(LInterval.Start()) + " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      return LInterval.Reg;
    end;

    // The moves joining two parts of a value inside a block, before the instruction the
    // later part starts at (a part starting at a block's start is the resolution's), each
    // position's sequenced
    hidden method DoSplitMoves();
    var
      LParts: ref Int64List;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LAt: int64;
      LG: int64;
      LV: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LV := 0 to self.FFunction.VRegCount - 1 do
        if self.FResident[LV] then
          skip;
        end;
        LParts := self.FPartsOf[LV];
        for LI := 1 to LParts.Count - 1 do
          LAt := self.FIntervals[LParts[LI]].Start();
          if ((LAt mod 2) <> 0) or (LAt >= 2 * self.FInstrCount) then
            skip;
          end;
          LG := LAt div 2;
          if self.FFirst[self.FBlockOf[LG]] = LG then
            skip;
          end;
          LFrom := self.DoLocation(LV, LAt - 1);
          if LFrom = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE then
            skip;
          end;
          LTo := self.DoPartPlace(LParts[LI]);
          if LFrom <> LTo then
            if self.FMovesBefore[LG] = nil then
              self.FMovesBefore[LG] := ref MoveList();
            end;
            self.FMovesBefore[LG].Add(LV, LFrom, LTo);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      for LG := 0 to self.FInstrCount - 1 do
        if self.FMovesBefore[LG] <> nil then
          self.FMovesBefore[LG] := self.DoSequence(self.FMovesBefore[LG]);
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Each edge's moves (see the header): every value live into the successor (not kept in
    // its slot) from its place at the predecessor's end to its place at the successor's
    // start, sequenced, put at the predecessor's end, the successor's start or an edge block
    hidden method DoResolve();
    var
      LMoves: ref MoveList;
      LWord: uint64;
      LEdge: int64;
      LFrom: int64;
      LTo: int64;
      LNode: int64;
      LP: int64;
      LS: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LW: int64;
      LBit: int64;
      LV: int64;
    begin
      for LP := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        for LK := 0 to self.FSuccs[LP].Count - 1 do
          LS := self.FSuccs[LP][LK];
          LMoves := ref MoveList();
          for LW := 0 to self.FWords - 1 do
            LWord := self.FLiveIn[LS * self.FWords + LW];
            if LWord = 0 then
              skip;
            end;
            for LBit := 0 to 63 do
              if (LWord & (uint64(1) shl uint64(LBit))) = 0 then
                skip;
              end;
              LV := LW * 64 + LBit;
              if self.FResident[LV] then
                skip;
              end;
              LFrom := self.DoLocation(LV, self.FTo[LP] - 1);
              LTo := self.DoLocation(LV, self.FFrom[LS]);
              if (LFrom = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE) or (LTo = ADAM_X64_ALLOC_NOWHERE) then
                raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_PLACE + self.DoVRegText(LV) + " on m" +
                  IntToStr(LP) + " -> m" + IntToStr(LS) + " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
              end;
              if LFrom <> LTo then
                LMoves.Add(LV, LFrom, LTo);
              end;
            end;
          end;
          if LMoves.Count() = 0 then
            skip;
          end;
          LMoves := self.DoSequence(LMoves);
          LNode := self.FInstrs[self.FFirst[LP] + (self.FTo[LP] - self.FFrom[LP]) div 2 - 1].Node;
          if self.FSuccs[LP].Count = 1 then
            self.FMovesEnd[LP] := LMoves;
          else
            if (self.FPredCount[LS] = 1) and (LS <> 0) then
              self.FMovesStart[LS] := LMoves;
            else
              LEdge := self.FFunction.AddBlock(0);
              if self.FFunction.BlockAt(LP).Source <> 0 then
                self.FFunction.BlockAt(LEdge).EdgeFrom := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LP).Source;
              else
                self.FFunction.BlockAt(LEdge).EdgeFrom := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LP).EdgeFrom;
              end;
              self.FFunction.BlockAt(LEdge).EdgeTo := self.FFunction.BlockAt(LS).Source;
              self.FEdgeBlocks.Add(LEdge);
              self.FEdgeTargets.Add(LS);
              self.FEdgeNodes.Add(LNode);
              setlength(self.FEdgeMoves, self.FEdgeBlocks.Count);
              self.FEdgeMoves[self.FEdgeBlocks.Count - 1] := LMoves;
              self.FRetargetFrom[LP].Add(LS);
              self.FRetargetTo[LP].Add(LEdge);
            end;
          end;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // The callee-saved registers an interval was given or selection writes, and a realigned
    // frame's frame register, into FSaved (general) and FSavedVector (vector) in the ABI's
    // order; raises for a frame register the ABI does not call saved
    hidden method DoSavedRegisters();
    var
      LWritten: BoolArray;
      LCalleeSaved: StringArray;
      LNumber: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LR: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LWritten, self.FRegisters);
      for LR := 0 to self.FRegisters - 1 do
        LWritten[LR] := self.FFixedWritten[LR];
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FIntervalCount - 1 do
        if self.FIntervals[LI].Reg >= 0 then
          LWritten[self.FIntervals[LI].Reg] := true;
        end;
      end;
      // A realigned frame writes its frame register in the prologue
      if self.FFrameReg >= 0 then
        if (self.FFrameReg = self.FStack) or (self.FFrameReg >= ADAM_X64_FIRST_XMM) then
          raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_FRAME_REGISTER + self.FRegisterTable.Text(self.FFrameReg));
        end;
        LWritten[self.FFrameReg] := true;
      end;
      LCalleeSaved := self.FAbi.CalleeSaved();
      for LI := 0 to len(LCalleeSaved) - 1 do
        LNumber := self.DoPhysical(LCalleeSaved[LI]);
        if (LNumber <> self.FStack) and LWritten[LNumber] then
          if LNumber >= ADAM_X64_FIRST_XMM then
            self.FSavedVector.Add(LNumber);
          else
            self.FSaved.Add(LNumber);
          end;
        end;
      end;
      if (self.FFrameReg >= 0) and (self.FSaved.IndexOf(self.FFrameReg) < 0) then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_FRAME_REGISTER + self.FRegisterTable.Text(self.FFrameReg));
      end;
    end;

    // Every slot placed (the spill slots are made by now), the frame from the ABI's rule
    hidden method DoFrame();
    var
      LOffsets: Int64Array;
      LPos: int64;
      LAlign: int64;
      LOutgoing: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      // The locals: each slot at its alignment, in order, from 0
      setlength(LOffsets, self.FFunction.SlotCount);
      LPos := 0;
      LAlign := 1;
      for LI := 0 to self.FFunction.SlotCount - 1 do
        LPos := DoRoundUp(LPos, self.FFunction.SlotAlign(LI));
        LOffsets[LI] := LPos;
        LPos := LPos + self.FFunction.SlotSize(LI);
        if self.FFunction.SlotAlign(LI) > LAlign then
          LAlign := self.FFunction.SlotAlign(LI);
        end;
      end;
      LOutgoing := 0;
      if self.FFunction.MakesCalls then
        LOutgoing := self.FFunction.OutgoingBytes;
      end;
      self.FFrame := self.FAbi.LayoutFrame(LPos, LAlign, LOutgoing, self.FSaved.Count,
        self.FSavedVector.Count, self.FFunction.MakesCalls);
      // The ABI realigns exactly when DoFrameRegister reserved its frame register
      if (self.FFrame.Realign > 0) <> (self.FFrameReg >= 0) then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_REALIGN + self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      if (self.FFrameReg >= 0) and
        (self.DoPhysical(self.FFrame.FrameRegister) <> self.FFrameReg) then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_REALIGN + self.FFunction.Symbol + ": " +
          self.FFrame.FrameRegister);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FFunction.SlotCount - 1 do
        self.FFunction.PlaceSlot(LI, self.FFrame.LocalBase + LOffsets[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // Place APlace of virtual register AVReg as an operand: the register, or its spill slot
    // off the stack pointer
    hidden method DoPlaceOperand(const AVReg: int64; const APlace: int64): ref MachineOperand;
    begin
      if APlace >= 0 then
        return PhysicalOperand(APlace);
      end;
      return RegisterMemory(self.FStack, false, self.FFunction.SlotOffset(self.FSlotOf[AVReg]));
    end;

    // A move of virtual register AVReg from place AFrom to place ATo: 8 bytes (a general
    // register whole, a vector one's float64)
    hidden method DoMoveInstr(const AVReg: int64; const AFrom: int64; const ATo: int64;
      const ANode: int64): ref MachineInstr;
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      if self.FFunction.VRegClass(AVReg) = RegClass.Vector then
        LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.MovSD, 0, ANode);
      else
        LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Mov, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      end;
      LInstr.AddOperand(self.DoPlaceOperand(AVReg, ATo));
      LInstr.AddOperand(self.DoPlaceOperand(AVReg, AFrom));
      return LInstr;
    end;

    // The sequenced AMoves at the end of ABlock
    hidden method DoEmitMoves(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const AMoves: ref MoveList;
      const ANode: int64);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to AMoves.Count() - 1 do
        ABlock.AddInstr(self.DoMoveInstr(AMoves.VRegs[LI], AMoves.Froms[LI], AMoves.Tos[LI],
          ANode));
      end;
    end;

    // The register virtual register AVReg is in at APos; raises when it is in none there
    hidden method DoRegisterAt(const AVReg: int64; const APos: int64): int64;
    var
      LPlace: int64;
    begin
      LPlace := self.DoLocation(AVReg, APos);
      if LPlace < 0 then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_NO_PLACE + self.DoVRegText(AVReg) + " at " + IntToStr(APos) +
          " in " + self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      return LPlace;
    end;

    // Operand AIndex of AInstr (number AG, of block ABlock) over physical registers and the
    // stack pointer: a virtual register (or base) is its register there, a jump target sent
    // to an edge block is that block, a slot and the incoming and outgoing areas are places
    // off the stack pointer after the prologue, a memory index its register there too
    hidden method DoResolveOperand(const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const AIndex: int64;
      const AG: int64; const ABlock: int64): ref MachineOperand;
    var
      LOperand: ref MachineOperand;
      LMemory: ref MachineOperand;
      LPos: int64;
      LK: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LOperand := AInstr.OperandAt(AIndex);
      if LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.VirtualReg then
        // Read and written: one place (no split inside an instruction)
        LPos := 2 * AG + 1;
        if X64OperandReads(AInstr, AIndex) then
          LPos := 2 * AG;
        end;
        return PhysicalOperand(self.DoRegisterAt(LOperand.Reg, LPos));
      end;
      if LOperand.Kind = OperandKind.BlockRef then
        LK := self.FRetargetFrom[ABlock].IndexOf(LOperand.Block);
        if LK >= 0 then
          return BlockOperand(self.FRetargetTo[ABlock][LK]);
        end;
        return LOperand;
      end;
      if LOperand.Kind <> OperandKind.Memory then
        return LOperand;
      end;
      LMemory := self.DoResolveMemory(LOperand, AG);
      if LOperand.Scale > 0 then
        // The index: its register there (read, as the base), else the physical one it names
        LIndex := LOperand.IndexReg;
        if LOperand.IndexVirtual then
          LIndex := self.DoRegisterAt(LOperand.IndexReg, 2 * AG);
        end;
        return IndexedMemory(LMemory, LIndex, false, LOperand.Scale);
      end;
      return LMemory;
    end;

    // Memory operand AOperand of instruction number AG without its index, over physical
    // registers and the stack pointer (DoResolveOperand)
    hidden method DoResolveMemory(const AOperand: ref MachineOperand;
      const AG: int64): ref MachineOperand;
    var
      LOperand: ref MachineOperand;
      LMemory: ref MachineOperand;
    begin
      LOperand := AOperand;
      match LOperand.Base of
        MemoryBase.Slot:
          return RegisterMemory(self.FStack, false,
            self.FFunction.SlotOffset(LOperand.SlotIndex) + LOperand.Disp);
        MemoryBase.Incoming:
          // A realigned frame's incoming area is off its frame register (the stack pointer
          // moved by an amount known only at run time)
          if self.FFrameReg >= 0 then
            return RegisterMemory(self.FFrameReg, false, self.FFrame.EntryBase + LOperand.Disp);
          end;
          return RegisterMemory(self.FStack, false, self.FFrame.EntryBase + LOperand.Disp);
        MemoryBase.Outgoing:
          return RegisterMemory(self.FStack, false, LOperand.Disp);
        MemoryBase.Register:
          if LOperand.BaseVirtual then
            LMemory := RegisterMemory(self.DoRegisterAt(LOperand.Reg, 2 * AG), false,
              LOperand.Disp);
            LMemory.DispSymbol := LOperand.DispSymbol;
            LMemory.DispKind := LOperand.DispKind;
            return LMemory;
          end;
        MemoryBase.RipSymbol:
          return LOperand;
        MemoryBase.Segment:
          return LOperand;
      end;
      return LOperand;
    end;

    // AOp (sub in the prologue, add before a ret) of the frame's reserved bytes on the stack
    // pointer, at the end of ABlock
    hidden method DoStackAdjust(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const AOp: X64Op;
      const APrologue: bool; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(AOp, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FStack));
      LInstr.AddOperand(ImmediateOperand(self.FFrame.AllocBytes));
      LInstr.Prologue := APrologue;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
    end;

    // AInstr (number AG, of block ABlockIndex) at the end of ABlock over physical registers:
    // the values kept in their slot it reads loaded first, the instruction, the ones it
    // writes stored after it
    hidden method DoRewrite(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const AG: int64;
      const AInstr: ref MachineInstr; const ABlockIndex: int64);
    var
      LLoaded: ref Int64List;
      LNew: ref MachineInstr;
      LV: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LLoaded := nil;
      for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(AInstr) - 1 do
        LV := DoRefVReg(AInstr, LI);
        if (LV >= 0) and self.FResident[LV] and DoRefReads(AInstr, LI) then
          if LLoaded = nil then
            LLoaded := ref Int64List();
          end;
          if LLoaded.IndexOf(LV) < 0 then
            LLoaded.Add(LV);
            ABlock.AddInstr(self.DoMoveInstr(LV, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT,
              self.DoRegisterAt(LV, 2 * AG), AInstr.Node));
          end;
        end;
      end;
      LNew := ref MachineInstr(AInstr.Op, AInstr.Width, AInstr.Node);
      LNew.Cond := AInstr.Cond;
      LNew.ImplicitUses := AInstr.ImplicitUses;
      LNew.ImplicitDefs := AInstr.ImplicitDefs;
      LNew.Prologue := AInstr.Prologue;
      for LI := 0 to AInstr.OperandCount - 1 do
        LNew.AddOperand(self.DoResolveOperand(AInstr, LI, AG, ABlockIndex));
      end;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LNew);
      for LI := 0 to DoRefCount(AInstr) - 1 do
        LV := DoRefVReg(AInstr, LI);
        if (LV >= 0) and self.FResident[LV] and DoRefWrites(AInstr, LI) then
          ABlock.AddInstr(self.DoMoveInstr(LV, self.DoRegisterAt(LV, 2 * AG + 1),
            ADAM_X64_ALLOC_IN_SLOT, AInstr.Node));
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // Block AIndex rewritten (see the header): the prologue at the entry's start, a
    // single predecessor's edge moves, then per instruction the split moves before it, the
    // edge moves before the closing jumps, a ret's epilogue, the instruction itself
    hidden method DoBlock(const AIndex: int64);
    var
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LOld: InstrArray;
      LCount: int64;
      LFirst: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LR: int64;
    begin
      LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(AIndex);
      LCount := LBlock.InstrCount;
      setlength(LOld, LCount);
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        LOld[LI] := LBlock.InstrAt(LI);
      end;
      LBlock.Clear();
      if AIndex = 0 then
        // The prologue: the saves first (the frame rule's order), then a probed frame's
        // probe, then the reservation, then a realigned frame's frame register and the
        // rounding
        for LR := 0 to self.FSaved.Count - 1 do
          self.DoSaveMove(LBlock, X64Op.Push, self.FSaved[LR], true, self.FFunction.Node);
        end;
        if self.FFrame.ProbeBytes > 0 then
          self.DoProbe(LBlock, self.FFunction.Node);
        end;
        if self.FFrame.AllocBytes > 0 then
          self.DoStackAdjust(LBlock, X64Op.Sub, true, self.FFunction.Node);
        end;
        // The vector saves off the stack pointer after the reservation (before a realigned
        // frame's frame register takes it: still the same value then)
        for LR := 0 to self.FSavedVector.Count - 1 do
          self.DoVectorMove(LBlock, LR, self.FStack, true, self.FFunction.Node);
        end;
        if self.FFrameReg >= 0 then
          self.DoRealign(LBlock, self.FFunction.Node);
        end;
      end;
      if (self.FMovesStart[AIndex] <> nil) and (LCount > 0) then
        self.DoEmitMoves(LBlock, self.FMovesStart[AIndex], LOld[0].Node);
      end;
      LFirst := self.FFirst[AIndex];
      for LI := 0 to LCount - 1 do
        if self.FMovesBefore[LFirst + LI] <> nil then
          self.DoEmitMoves(LBlock, self.FMovesBefore[LFirst + LI], LOld[LI].Node);
        end;
        if (LI = self.FTrail[AIndex]) and (self.FMovesEnd[AIndex] <> nil) then
          self.DoEmitMoves(LBlock, self.FMovesEnd[AIndex], LOld[LI].Node);
        end;
        if (LOld[LI].Op = X64Op.Ret) or (LOld[LI].Op = X64Op.TailJmp) then
          // The epilogue: the prologue undone in reverse (a realigned frame releases off its
          // frame register, the one release form unwind data allows with one); a tail call's
          // jump leaves through it as a ret does. The vector saves come back first (off the
          // frame register in a realigned frame: the stack pointer was rounded)
          for LR := self.FSavedVector.Count - 1 downto 0 do
            if self.FFrameReg >= 0 then
              self.DoVectorMove(LBlock, LR, self.FFrameReg, false, LOld[LI].Node);
            else
              self.DoVectorMove(LBlock, LR, self.FStack, false, LOld[LI].Node);
            end;
          end;
          if self.FFrameReg >= 0 then
            self.DoRelease(LBlock, LOld[LI].Node);
          end;
          if (self.FFrameReg < 0) and (self.FFrame.AllocBytes > 0) then
            self.DoStackAdjust(LBlock, X64Op.Add, false, LOld[LI].Node);
          end;
          for LR := self.FSaved.Count - 1 downto 0 do
            self.DoSaveMove(LBlock, X64Op.Pop, self.FSaved[LR], false, LOld[LI].Node);
          end;
        end;
        self.DoRewrite(LBlock, LFirst + LI, LOld[LI], AIndex);
      end;
    end;

    // Edge block AK of the resolution: its moves, then a jump on to its target
    hidden method DoEdgeBlock(const AK: int64);
    var
      LBlock: ref MachineBlock;
      LJump: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      LBlock := self.FFunction.BlockAt(self.FEdgeBlocks[AK]);
      self.DoEmitMoves(LBlock, self.FEdgeMoves[AK], self.FEdgeNodes[AK]);
      LJump := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Jmp, 0, self.FEdgeNodes[AK]);
      LJump.AddOperand(BlockOperand(self.FEdgeTargets[AK]));
      LBlock.AddInstr(LJump);
    end;

    // A push (in the prologue) or a pop (before a ret) of callee-saved register AReg, at the
    // end of ABlock
    hidden method DoSaveMove(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const AOp: X64Op; const AReg: int64;
      const APrologue: bool; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(AOp, 0, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(AReg));
      LInstr.Prologue := APrologue;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
    end;

    // The save (in the prologue: movaps [base + VectorBase + 16 * AK], xmm) or the restore
    // (before a ret: movaps xmm, [base + ...]) of the AK-th saved vector register, off ABase
    // (the stack pointer, or a realigned frame's frame register), at the end of ABlock
    hidden method DoVectorMove(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const AK: int64;
      const ABase: int64; const ASave: bool; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LPlace: ref MachineOperand;
    begin
      LPlace := RegisterMemory(ABase, false, self.FFrame.VectorBase +
        AK * ADAM_X64_ALLOC_VECTOR_SAVE_BYTES);
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.MovAps, 0, ANode);
      if ASave then
        LInstr.AddOperand(LPlace);
        LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FSavedVector[AK]));
      else
        LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FSavedVector[AK]));
        LInstr.AddOperand(LPlace);
      end;
      LInstr.Prologue := ASave;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
    end;

    // A realigned frame's end of prologue, at the end of ABlock: mov frame, rsp (a prologue
    // instruction: the frame register's step), then and rsp, -Realign (after the prologue:
    // unwind data reaches the frame through the frame register from here on)
    hidden method DoRealign(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Mov, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FFrameReg));
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FStack));
      LInstr.Prologue := true;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.BitAnd, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FStack));
      LInstr.AddOperand(ImmediateOperand(0 - self.FFrame.Realign));
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
    end;

    // A probed frame's probe, at the end of ABlock (after the pushes): mov size, ProbeBytes;
    // call the probe (see the header); a probe register live into the function raises
    hidden method DoProbe(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LScratch: ref Int64List;
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LScratch := ProbeRegisters(self.FAbi, self.FRegisterTable);
      for LI := 0 to LScratch.Count - 1 do
        if self.FEntryLive[LScratch[LI]] then
          raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_PROBE_LIVE + self.FFunction.Symbol + ": " +
            self.FRegisterTable.Text(LScratch[LI]));
        end;
      end;
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Mov, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(LScratch[0]));
      LInstr.AddOperand(ImmediateOperand(self.FFrame.ProbeBytes));
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Call, 0, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(SymbolOperand(SymbolClass.Code, ADAM_X64_PROBE_SYMBOL));
      LInstr.ImplicitUses.Add(LScratch[0]);
      for LI := 0 to LScratch.Count - 1 do
        LInstr.ImplicitDefs.Add(LScratch[LI]);
      end;
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
      // The function calls (the probe needs no outgoing area: the frame stands as laid out)
      self.FFunction.MakesCalls := true;
    end;

    // A realigned frame's release before a ret's pops, at the end of ABlock:
    // lea rsp, [frame + AllocBytes] (the stack pointer as it was before the reservation)
    hidden method DoRelease(const ABlock: ref MachineBlock; const ANode: int64);
    var
      LInstr: ref MachineInstr;
    begin
      LInstr := ref MachineInstr(X64Op.Lea, ADAM_X64_ALLOC_SPILL_BYTES, ANode);
      LInstr.AddOperand(PhysicalOperand(self.FStack));
      LInstr.AddOperand(RegisterMemory(self.FFrameReg, false, self.FFrame.AllocBytes));
      ABlock.AddInstr(LInstr);
    end;

    // "v3" / "x3": virtual register AVReg as Dump names it
    hidden method DoVRegText(const AVReg: int64): string;
    begin
      if self.FFunction.VRegClass(AVReg) = RegClass.Vector then
        return "x" + IntToStr(AVReg);
      end;
      return "v" + IntToStr(AVReg);
    end;

    // The function allocated (see the header)
    method Run();
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if self.FFunction.Frame <> nil then
        raise(ADAM_X64_ALLOC_FAULT_TWICE + self.FFunction.Symbol);
      end;
      self.DoRegisters();
      self.DoFrameRegister();
      self.DoCandidates();
      self.DoCloseBlocks();
      self.DoCfg();
      self.DoNumber();
      self.DoLiveness();
      self.DoFixed();
      self.DoIntervals();
      self.DoPieces();
      self.DoWalk();
      self.DoSplitMoves();
      self.DoResolve();
      self.DoSavedRegisters();
      self.DoFrame();
      for LI := 0 to self.FBlockCount - 1 do
        self.DoBlock(LI);
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FEdgeBlocks.Count - 1 do
        self.DoEdgeBlock(LI);
      end;
      self.FFunction.Frame := self.FFrame;
    end;
  end;

// AFunction (selected, not yet allocated) allocated in place: registers numbered by
// Adam.X64.Registers, the candidates and the frame from AAbi (see the header); raises for a
// function it cannot allocate and for a register AAbi names that x86_64 lacks
public func AllocateFunction(const AFunction: ref MachineFunction; const AAbi: ref AbiPart);
var
  LAllocator: ref Allocator;
begin
  LAllocator := ref Allocator(AFunction, AAbi);
  LAllocator.Run();
end;

end.
